#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124205 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "ccfdc303-534f-530e-810b-f475a997f5d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4703" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its pivot columns?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124206 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "22a77802-4114-516f-a0e0-4cda2e069361" :question/math-academy-id "e-4704" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $C$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $C$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124207 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "6e4b2e85-86a8-5050-a60a-ae8d40453ad0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4705" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124208 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "3ac076bd-5add-5c08-bb96-7b11c0a37d54" :question/math-academy-id "e-4706" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{2}{7}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "287b38ee-41c7-5532-a8a3-471340d911f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308369} {:answer/id #uuid "63026364-bf1b-50ac-b117-cbf42d7f36cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308370} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb0ec5a-6781-5d33-9e7b-73e42215938b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308371} {:answer/id #uuid "ee04422b-9124-56c2-9b98-4a81d3395c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308372} {:answer/id #uuid "2f74ad50-7430-5dbc-84ac-d80c7e1bcc93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bb0ec5a-6781-5d33-9e7b-73e42215938b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308371} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dc3303f-95e7-5c89-89c5-b3b31b1ac3ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c3953ab-7f0d-5e25-8ad2-b067a76cac57" :question/math-academy-id "q-130953" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $2$nd and $5$th columns."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46788460-a906-5bca-a473-0d50e4dd04c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308376} {:answer/id #uuid "1353b547-c5f2-5e96-b0c6-fd7821416157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308377} {:answer/id #uuid "d112678a-1277-54b3-950c-53f665aeb64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308378} {:answer/id #uuid "6c7a257a-a983-5ab5-90ec-d315c00bf115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308379} {:answer/id #uuid "1f11a06a-7ddd-5407-ba94-05bf8a729e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46788460-a906-5bca-a473-0d50e4dd04c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308376} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ca6e6b4-0a47-591a-849e-8e293ca83953" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cff88abe-cb9f-5f2b-aa6a-898f213ad5e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130955" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56a1be4b-fce1-5dec-8df0-3d03c9aeea65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308383} {:answer/id #uuid "f05bb5bf-1451-5ade-8d4c-0c58667e2ebd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308384} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd3b7d1-db8b-5d4e-bc95-f47b7fee4693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308385} {:answer/id #uuid "249050c7-1c59-57a9-9d4b-755160ad5fb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308386} {:answer/id #uuid "537e5983-52ef-54f1-a1f5-7e9833b365f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56a1be4b-fce1-5dec-8df0-3d03c9aeea65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308383} :answer-field/id #uuid "65b75c9f-b4d2-5418-982e-deaf4f0f3144" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d95bf93e-1450-553f-9ef8-b9be3aa5bf3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130957" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186322404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cf0c341-bb64-53ac-b1b5-fbd0f2861558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322406} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e001fa-5cce-5139-b479-b668b154bec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322407} {:answer/id #uuid "f163575b-0b5f-515a-abcd-7193bfaecbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322408} {:answer/id #uuid "c8fb0641-3a3d-5afa-9248-bb58e8e3ac51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322409} {:answer/id #uuid "34a1fbec-7497-5269-9261-b82398df7161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf0c341-bb64-53ac-b1b5-fbd0f2861558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322406} :answer-field/id #uuid "eeed0805-e25a-5df2-a5ba-04f91d32ca10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2cb7299f-8b80-5020-a0a1-407df3d0dba1" :question/math-academy-id "q-130958" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308402 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "feaf37d9-9ed3-5ee2-8818-b14b8ccbbd56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308404} {:answer/id #uuid "535afafc-e10d-5eb2-bc92-5dd77118c720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308405} {:answer/id #uuid "682a828a-6a0c-5f67-939e-a2de891109d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308406} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f2567e-7e0a-51e7-b569-d3490577a2fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218630840